      "source_line": "| 1828 | 30002726 / OWR-13353-012 | Complexity of Maximizing Initial Odd Ears | 0.0536 | 5.0 | 3 | 2014 | claimed_solved | 3/5 |  | 2026-10-20: CLAIMED_SOLVED after 3/5 substantive approaches. Deciding beta(G)>=t for variable input threshold t is NP-complete even for simple 2-vertex-connected universal-apex graphs whose apex deletion is connected bipartite. Beta counts the initial consecutive odd ears in an open ear decomposition, including the initial circuit and one-edge ears. Complete Set Cover reduction and independent mathematical audit PASS; primary proof bytes preserved. Exact isolated standard-library replay: 63 subset instances, 14 cones, 1719 threshold decisions over 441 systems, zero discrepancies. Proof, audit, acceptance report and public provenance in [initial_odd_ears_30002726](../initial_odd_ears_30002726/README.md). No fixed-threshold or total-odd-ear hardness, novelty certification, or external-peer-review claim. |  |",
